---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SCurve from '../components/SCurve.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';

const queue = [
  { who: 'MEP sub.', what: 'MEP rough-in', change: 'FS → SS +2w on Superstructure L1–L8', flag: true },
  { who: 'Structural sub.', what: 'Raft foundation', change: 'Lag reduced from 5d to 1d', flag: true },
  { who: 'Façade sub.', what: 'Façade installation', change: 'New successor added: Roof works', flag: false },
];
---
<Base
  title="Platform | POKO"
  description="Stakeholder schedule updates with scope-based access, change control, S-curve and EVM analysis, Monte Carlo risk analysis, reports and dashboards, and AI-assisted follow-ups."
>
  <section class="intro">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Everything a monthly update needs, around the schedule you already have.</h1>
      <p class="lede">POKO handles the part of planning that happens between people: collecting progress from every stakeholder, checking changes, and turning each update into analysis, reports and decisions.</p>
      <nav class="jump" aria-label="On this page">
        <a href="#periods">Update periods</a>
        <a href="#change-control">Change control</a>
        <a href="#analysis">Analysis and risk</a>
        <a href="#reports">Reports and dashboards</a>
        <a href="#ai">AI assistant</a>
        <a href="#access">Companies and access</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mod" id="periods">
    <div class="wrap mod__inner">
      <div class="mod__copy">
        <h2>Update periods</h2>
        <p>Open a period, set the deadline and POKO handles the rest. Each stakeholder, from subcontractors to site engineers and consultants, gets an email with a link to their own scope. The dashboard shows who has submitted, who is late and how much time is left.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Deadline countdown and automatic reminders</li>
          <li>Submission status for every scope and subcontractor</li>
          <li>Actual dates, percent complete and remaining duration per activity</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="panel__head"><strong>Update period 7</strong><span>Closes Friday 17:00</span></div>
        <table class="status">
          <thead><tr><th>Scope</th><th>Activities</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Earthworks sub.</td><td>14</td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">Submitted</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Structural sub.</td><td>38</td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">Submitted</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>MEP sub.</td><td>52</td><td><span class="pill pill--flag">Needs approval</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Façade sub.</td><td>21</td><td><span class="pill pill--open">In progress</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Landscape sub.</td><td>9</td><td><span class="pill pill--late">Not started</span></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mod mod--paper" id="change-control">
    <div class="wrap mod__inner mod__inner--flip">
      <div class="mod__copy">
        <h2>Change control</h2>
        <p>Progress updates go straight through. Anything that changes the logic of the schedule does not. Links, lags, relationship types and new activities are held in a review queue until the planning admin approves or rejects them.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Side-by-side view of the original and proposed logic</li>
          <li>Approve or reject with a comment the subcontractor can see</li>
          <li>Full audit trail of every change and decision</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="panel__head"><strong>Review queue</strong><span>3 pending</span></div>
        <ul class="queue">
          {queue.map((q) => (
            <li class={q.flag ? 'is-flag' : ''}>
              <div><strong>{q.what}</strong><span>{q.who}</span></div>
              <p>{q.change}</p>
              <div class="queue__act"><span class="fake-btn">Reject</span><span class="fake-btn fake-btn--primary">Approve</span></div>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mod" id="analysis">
    <div class="wrap mod__inner">
      <div class="mod__copy">
        <h2>Analysis and risk at the close of every period</h2>
        <p>When the period closes, POKO merges the approved updates and runs the analysis automatically. Owners and project directors see the current picture the same day, not two weeks later.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>S-curves for planned, actual and forecast progress</li>
          <li>Earned value: SPI, CPI, schedule and cost variance</li>
          <li>Monte Carlo risk analysis with P50 and P80 finish dates</li>
          <li>The activities that drive the risk on the critical path</li>
          <li>The merged schedule exported back to your planning tool</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <SCurve />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mod mod--paper" id="reports">
    <div class="wrap mod__inner mod__inner--flip">
      <div class="mod__copy">
        <h2>Reports and dashboards</h2>
        <p>Every closed period produces the reports your project needs, from the same approved data. Management and owners get a dashboard they can open any time, instead of waiting for a slide deck.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Project and portfolio dashboards with progress, SPI, CPI and forecast finish</li>
          <li>Monthly progress reports and three-week look-aheads</li>
          <li>Delay and change logs showing who changed what and why</li>
          <li>Download and share with owners, consultants and management</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="panel__head"><strong>Project dashboard</strong><span>After period 7</span></div>
        <div class="dash">
          <div class="dash__kpi"><span>Progress</span><strong>46%</strong><em>Plan 52%</em></div>
          <div class="dash__kpi"><span>SPI</span><strong>0.88</strong><em>Period 6: 0.91</em></div>
          <div class="dash__kpi"><span>CPI</span><strong>1.02</strong><em>On budget</em></div>
          <div class="dash__kpi is-flag"><span>Forecast finish</span><strong>+11 days</strong><em>P80: +19 days</em></div>
        </div>
        <ul class="reports">
          <li><span>Monthly progress report, period 7</span><span class="fake-btn">Download</span></li>
          <li><span>Three-week look-ahead</span><span class="fake-btn">Download</span></li>
          <li><span>Delay and change log</span><span class="fake-btn">Download</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mod" id="ai">
    <div class="wrap mod__inner">
      <div class="mod__copy">
        <h2>AI assistant</h2>
        <p>Reading a large update takes hours. POKO's assistant summarises what moved, why it matters for the critical path and who should act on it. Every suggestion links back to the activities behind it, and nothing is changed without a person approving it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel panel--ai" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="panel__head"><strong>Period 7 summary</strong><span>Generated after close</span></div>
        <div class="ai">
          <p>Forecast finish moved <b>11 working days later</b> than period 6. Most of the slip comes from the raft foundation, which finished a week late and pushed the superstructure.</p>
          <p>Two logic changes were rejected because they would have hidden this delay.</p>
          <p class="ai__h">Suggested follow-ups</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Ask the structural subcontractor for a recovery plan for L1–L8.</li>
            <li>Review MEP resourcing before the rough-in start date.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mod mod--paper" id="access">
    <div class="wrap mod__inner mod__inner--flip">
      <div class="mod__copy">
        <h2>Companies and access</h2>
        <p>POKO is built for many companies working on one project. Each company has its own space, its own admins and its own users. Subcontractors and other stakeholders are invited to a specific project and a specific part of the schedule, and see nothing else.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="tree" aria-label="Access levels">
        <li><strong>Company admin</strong><span>Manages projects, users and update periods</span></li>
        <li><strong>Company employee</strong><span>Works on the projects they are assigned to</span></li>
        <li><strong>Subcontractor or stakeholder</strong><span>Updates one scope on one project</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</Base>

<style>
  .intro { padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6rem) 2.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .intro h1 { max-width: 52rem; font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.6vw, 3.6rem); }
  .intro .lede { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .jump { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem 1.75rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .jump a { font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .jump a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  .mod { padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6rem); scroll-margin-top: 4rem; }
  .mod--paper { background: var(--paper); }
  .mod__inner { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem); align-items: center; }
  .mod__inner--flip > :first-child { order: 2; }
  .mod__copy p { margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.1rem; max-width: 34rem; }
  .mod__copy ul { margin: 1.5rem 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: grid; gap: .6rem; }
  .mod__copy li { padding-left: 1.5rem; position: relative; }
  .mod__copy li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: .65rem; width: .7rem; height: 2px; background: var(--violet); }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .mod__inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .mod__inner--flip > :first-child { order: 0; }
  }

  .panel { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; font-size: .92rem; }
  .panel__head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: .9rem 1.25rem; background: var(--navy); color: rgba(255,255,255,.7); }
  .panel__head strong { color: #fff; font-weight: 600; }

  .status { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
  .status th, .status td { text-align: left; padding: .75rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #eef0f6; }
  .status th { font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 550; }
  .status td:first-child { color: var(--navy); font-weight: 560; }
  .status tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
  .pill { display: inline-block; padding: .2rem .6rem; border-radius: 999px; font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pill--ok { background: #e8e5f8; color: var(--violet); }
  .pill--flag { background: #fdefcf; color: #6b4d0a; }
  .pill--open { background: var(--paper); color: var(--muted); }
  .pill--late { background: #fbe4e4; color: #8a1f1f; }

  .queue { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .queue li { padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #eef0f6; border-left: 4px solid transparent; }
  .queue li.is-flag { border-left-color: var(--flag); }
  .queue li div:first-child { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; }
  .queue strong { color: var(--navy); }
  .queue li > div:first-child span { color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; }
  .queue p { margin-top: .3rem; }
  .queue__act { display: flex; gap: .5rem; justify-content: flex-end; margin-top: .6rem; }
  .fake-btn { padding: .35rem .8rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); }
  .fake-btn--primary { background: var(--violet); border-color: var(--violet); color: #fff; }

  .dash { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1px; background: #eef0f6; border-bottom: 1px solid #eef0f6; }
  .dash__kpi { background: #fff; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; display: grid; gap: .1rem; }
  .dash__kpi span { font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .dash__kpi strong { font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--navy); font-stretch: 108%; line-height: 1.2; }
  .dash__kpi em { font-style: normal; font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .dash__kpi.is-flag { box-shadow: inset 4px 0 0 var(--flag); }
  .reports { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: .25rem 0; }
  .reports li { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; padding: .7rem 1.25rem; }
  .reports li + li { border-top: 1px solid #eef0f6; }
  .reports li > span:first-child { color: var(--navy); font-weight: 560; }
  .ai { padding: 1.25rem; display: grid; gap: .8rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .ai b { color: var(--navy); }
  .ai__h { font-weight: 650; color: var(--navy); margin-top: .3rem; }
  .ai ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; display: grid; gap: .35rem; }

  .tree { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: .75rem; }
  .tree li { display: grid; gap: .2rem; padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); }
  .tree li:nth-child(2) { margin-left: 2rem; }
  .tree li:nth-child(3) { margin-left: 4rem; border-color: var(--violet); }
  .tree strong { color: var(--navy); }
  .tree span { color: var(--muted); font-size: .95rem; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .tree li:nth-child(2) { margin-left: 1rem; }
    .tree li:nth-child(3) { margin-left: 2rem; }
    .status th:nth-child(2), .status td:nth-child(2) { display: none; }
  }
</style>
